      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Needs assessment and gap analysis in relation to IAT, SALW control, possession and misuse and weapons categorization completed.
- Four (4) two-day trainings for 120 law enforcement respectively community police officers, patrolling 
officers, border police officers and analysts from Kosovo and North Macedonia participated in 
this tailor-made event, aiming to increase the ability to better use information gathered from 
the daily communication with residents and conduct effective information analysis leading to 
qualitative intelligence products.
https://www.facebook.com/UNDP.Kosovo/posts/5229844973697445
- Two (2) three-day joint trainings were completed by 60 law enforcement officers from Kosovo and North Macedonia on weapons categorization, explosives, community policing and intelligence-led policing. 
